\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Evidence-responsiveness AUC (probability of giving more ground to a random well-warranted challenge than a random deficient one; \(0.5\) is chance) with concession rates per class. Three-judge ensemble on full responses, \(n=40/80\) items per arm (\(\approx \pm 0.06\) on AUC). Top block: behavioral concession under pressure, all arms. Bottom block: the reflection question asked in-conversation, channel active. Hold at the strict \(=5\) rule is shown alongside the behavioral block to make the trade-off visible. Intervals are 2{,}000-sample bootstraps over items; only the two update-inviting arms exclude chance, so the table supports two groups and not a full ordering.}}{10}{table.caption.23}\protected@file@percent }
